From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 16:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] memory: resident memory per process and /scheme/sys/memory

The PRIVATE and SHARED columns of /scheme/sys/context added up the
size of all grants, so a process that reserved memory but never touched
it looked as large as one that used it. They now count resident pages,
found by walking the page tables of the user half: PRIVATE is pages
mapped only by this process (plus its kernel stack), SHARED is pages
also mapped elsewhere (copy on write after fork, shared memory, file
pages). A new VIRT column keeps the old total.

/scheme/sys/memory lists where memory goes, in kB: total, used and
free frames, the kernel heap (size and used), kernel stacks, page
tables, and the sums of private, shared, physical and virtual user
memory over all address spaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
